Reiss's slides for each day are typically drawn from these slidedecks organized by topic:

- [intro](slides/intro.pdf)
- [logistics](slides/logistics.pdf) (course logistics, might not be updated for current semester)
- [building](slides/building.pdf)
- [accounts](slides/accounts.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/accounts.pdf)</sup>
- [kernel](slides/kernel.pdf) (including exceptions)
- [signals](slides/signals.pdf) (Unix signals, now typically not covered)
- [unix-api](slides/unix-api.pdf) (fork, dup2, etc)
- [vm](slides/vm.pdf) (virtual memory)
- [caching](slides/caching.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/caching.pdf)</sup>
  *  [caching-blocking](slides/caching-blocking.html)<sup>(slides/caching-blocking.pdf)</sup> (cache blocking; typically not covered)
- [threads](slides/threads.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/threads.pdf)</sup>
- synchronization --
  *  [sync-reorder](slides/sync-reorder.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-reorder.pdf)</sup> (race conditions; interleaving; compiler/processor reordering)
      *  [sync-cc](slides/sync-cc.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-cc.pdf)</sup> (cache coherency; typically not covered)
  *  [sync-locks](slides/sync-locks.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-locks.pdf)</sup> (mutex-type locks)
     *  [sync-lock-impl](slides/sync-lock-impl.html)<sup>[pdf](sync-lock-impl.pdf)</sup> (implementation; typically not covered)
  *  [sync-barriers](slides/sync-barriers.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-barriers.pdf)</sup>
  *  [sync-monitors](slides/sync-monitors.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-monitors.pdf)</sup>
  *  [sync-false-share](slides/sync-false-share.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-false-share.pdf)</sup>
  *  [sync-rwlocks](slides/sync-rwlocks.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-rwlocks.pdf)</sup> (reader-writer locks)
  *  [sync-semaphores](slides/sync-semaphores.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-semaphores.pdf)</sup> (typically not covered)
  *  [sync-xact](slides/sync-xact.html)<sup>[pdf](slides/sync-xact.pdf)</sup> (transactions, very briefly)
- [deadlock](slides/deadlock.pdf) 
- [network](slides/network.pdf) 
- [secure](slides/secure.pdf) (secure channels, cryptography)
- [pipeline](slides/pipeline.pdf) (pipelined processors)
- [ooo](slides/ooo.pdf) (out-of-order processors)
- [spectre](slides/spectre.pdf) (side-channels, Meltdown, Spectre)

- [bpred](slides/bpred.pdf) (branch prediction)

Note that these slidedecks frequently contain extra slides that will not be used in most semesters.
